                <pb facs="0356" n="284" sameAs="frus:frus1865p4/pg284"/>

                <head>Municipal Council of London, Canada West</head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>London, Canada West</placeName>, <date
                        ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1865-04-01">April 17, 1865</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>At a meeting of the corporation of the city of London, in the province of Canada,
                    held on the seventeenth day of April, in the year of our Lord 1865, the
                    following resolution was unanimously adopted:</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Resolved</hi>, That, in view of the lamentable
                    occurrence which has taken place in the neighboring nation of the United States,
                    by which their Chief Magistrate has been deprived of life by the hand of an
                    assassin, we, the corporation of the city of London, deem it incumbent upon us
                    to offer to our sorrowing neighbors this expression of our sympathy for the
                    great loss they have sustained, and our abhorrence of the act by which they have
                    been made to suffer.</p>
                <p>In testimony whereof, I, Daniel Class, esq., mayor of the said city of London,
                    have hereunto set my hand, and caused to be affixed the corporate seal of the
                    said city, on this eighteenth day of April, 1865.</p>
                <closer>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">seal</hi>.] <signed>DAVID GLASS, </signed>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mayor</hi>.</closer>
            </div>
